WEBVTT

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:04.630
﻿I never imagined that
﻿the boys you fought in Tokyo,

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:09.200
﻿would defeat Aila Jyrkiainen
﻿and advance to the final round.

00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:11.740
﻿Did you foresee this?

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:15.110
﻿I'm not that all-knowing.

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:20.720
﻿Working all night reminds me
﻿of being at the Gunpla Academy.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.420
﻿It was hard as hell.

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:24.590
﻿Even in my dreams,

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:27.120
﻿I still recall the second Meijin's words...

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:31.430
﻿Gunpla Battle is all about victory.

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:34.860
﻿Even if the opponent is
﻿your friend or sibling,

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:38.270
﻿you must push them
﻿out of your way to win.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:43.270
﻿Thanks to my severe experience
﻿at the Gunpla Academy,

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:45.270
﻿I succeeded as a builder.

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:48.210
﻿I'm grateful to the second Meijin.

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:50.950
﻿Of course, I'm grateful to him too.

00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:53.780
﻿For being a bad example.

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:56.450
﻿A bad example? What do you mean?

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:59.120
﻿Our semifinals opponent is...

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:01.290
﻿Sir John Ayers Mackenzie,
﻿representing the UK.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:03.490
﻿Y-Yeah.

00:01:03.490 --> 00:01:05.360
﻿He's 78 years old,

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:08.260
﻿the oldest contestant
﻿in the tournament.

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:08.830
﻿And...

00:01:09.470 --> 00:01:13.870
﻿a veteran fighter who fought
﻿deadly battles with the second Meijin.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:16.470
﻿Commodore Mackenzie!

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.040
﻿Oh, Lieutenant Ral.

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:20.780
﻿Long time no see.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:23.180
﻿Congratulations on
﻿advancing to the semifinals.

00:01:23.410 --> 00:01:26.620
﻿My opponent is the third Meijin.

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:28.720
﻿I must have a fateful
﻿connection with Meijins.

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:34.960
﻿M-My heart...!

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:37.560
﻿Commodore!? Hang in there!

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:40.960
﻿Commodore!

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:13.790
﻿Sei. Reiji.

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:17.800
﻿We brought you lunch
﻿that we made together.

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:21.440
﻿I thought you'd be fed up
﻿with meals in the players' village.

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:23.070
﻿Th-Thanks.

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:27.340
﻿- What's wrong?
- ﻿U-Um...

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:28.980
﻿Wow!!

00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:32.450
﻿Is that a Japanese "bento"!?

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:37.050
﻿I'm starving!

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:38.220
﻿Thank you.

00:03:41.190 --> 00:03:42.990
﻿Sh-She has nowhere else to go,

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:44.830
﻿so she suddenly moved in yesterday.

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:46.490
﻿No way!

00:03:46.630 --> 00:03:48.330
﻿Yeah, she can't stay here.

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:51.670
﻿You're going out with China, right?

00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:57.510
I didn't mean it that way...
﻿We're not...

00:03:57.510 --> 00:03:59.110
﻿The rice ball is yummy!

00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:00.910
﻿And she's just eating!

00:04:00.910 --> 00:04:04.010
﻿This is all chaos!

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:11.690
﻿Boys and girls in the same room?

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:13.850
﻿I can't allow that!

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:17.630
﻿So until the tournament ends,

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:20.790
﻿Aila will stay at
﻿the inn where I'm staying.

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:23.560
﻿And after that...

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:25.530
﻿I'll stay at Sei's house.

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:26.970
﻿What? Our house?

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:31.410
﻿Yeah. Reiji said if I had
﻿nowhere to go, I could stay at Sei's.

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:33.310
﻿Reiji.

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:36.710
﻿Why didn't you ask me first?

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:38.610
﻿Why not, Sei's mom?

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:43.050
﻿I'm sorry.
﻿If it's too much trouble...

00:04:45.350 --> 00:04:48.060
﻿I'm going to stay with you then.

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:49.690
﻿Why do you say that?

00:04:50.030 --> 00:04:52.530
﻿Take responsibility for your own words!

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:55.060
﻿It's no good.

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:57.200
﻿My home is in Arian.

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:59.270
﻿Arian?

00:04:59.330 --> 00:05:03.240
﻿It seems like Arian is the name
﻿of a country in another world.

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:07.240
﻿Reiji is a prince there, right?

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:08.080
﻿Huh?

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:10.210
﻿Is that true?

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:11.580
﻿Impressed?

00:05:15.950 --> 00:05:18.190
﻿Why don't you believe me!?

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:23.860
﻿Why don't you stay at the inn, too?

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:24.930
﻿Are you sure?

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:27.030
﻿The more, the merrier.

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:33.700
﻿Why does everyone laugh about it?

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:34.500
﻿So...

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:36.600
﻿Is it actually true?

00:05:36.610 --> 00:05:38.340
﻿Like I told you.

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:42.540
﻿Nils?

00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:45.580
﻿I'm sorry to interrupt you.

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:46.450
﻿What do you want?

00:05:47.210 --> 00:05:50.650
﻿I'd like to ask Reiji a favor.

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:51.390
﻿Me?

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:54.120
﻿What?

00:05:55.090 --> 00:05:57.990
﻿Reiji, during yesterday's battle...

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:01.560
﻿What's that light!?

00:06:01.930 --> 00:06:04.770
﻿What caused that phenomenon?

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:06.470
﻿About that?

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:08.340
﻿This rock glowed.

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:11.740
﻿That's...

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:18.110
﻿Would you please lend me
﻿that gem for a little while?

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:19.050
﻿No problem.

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:22.250
﻿Thanks, Reiji.

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:24.320
﻿Does that gem...

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:29.560
﻿have something to do with the secret
﻿of the Plavsky particle you're looking for?

00:06:29.560 --> 00:06:31.630
﻿I can't tell until I analyze it,

00:06:32.890 --> 00:06:35.560
﻿but I think it's possible.

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:41.340
﻿Grandpa!

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:43.240
﻿Julian?

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:45.270
﻿Lieutenant!

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:46.940
﻿Long time no see.

00:06:46.940 --> 00:06:49.140
﻿J-Julian...

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:50.810
﻿Grandpa!

00:06:51.280 --> 00:06:52.810
﻿Sorry I'm late.

00:06:52.810 --> 00:06:55.250
﻿No, thank you for coming all this way.

00:06:55.920 --> 00:06:58.150
﻿Sorry for the trouble.

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:02.560
﻿I'm relieved to see you're okay.

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:05.560
﻿I saw the championship on the news.

00:07:06.060 --> 00:07:08.100
﻿You've made it to the semifinals.

00:07:08.230 --> 00:07:13.000
﻿This is my first opportunity
﻿in my 78 years of life.

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:18.940
﻿But my next opponent is the Meijin.

00:07:19.340 --> 00:07:20.810
﻿The Meijin!?

00:07:20.810 --> 00:07:23.840
﻿Someone was chosen as
﻿the third generation?

00:07:23.850 --> 00:07:24.950
﻿Yes.

00:07:24.950 --> 00:07:28.520
﻿And he's too strong for me...

00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:31.520
﻿Grandpa!

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:33.520
﻿J-Julian...

00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:35.490
﻿I don't have much time left.

00:07:35.490 --> 00:07:36.790
﻿Don't say that.

00:07:38.530 --> 00:07:40.190
﻿Please take this.

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:44.260
﻿Fight in my place.

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:47.670
﻿Grandpa, I quit Gunpla Battle.

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:51.000
﻿This is my last wish.

00:07:51.970 --> 00:07:53.040
﻿Please.

00:07:53.440 --> 00:07:54.840
﻿Julian.

00:07:54.840 --> 00:08:00.510
﻿Win victory and honor
﻿for me and the Mackenzies!

00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:04.350
﻿Grandpa!?

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:07.250
﻿Grandpa!

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:10.190
﻿Please let him rest.

00:08:14.630 --> 00:08:17.100
﻿This is unfair, Grandpa.

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:18.530
﻿If you ask me like that,

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:20.700
﻿I can't decline your request.

00:08:21.370 --> 00:08:23.940
﻿And the battle is tomorrow.

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:26.810
﻿I don't even know
﻿what Gunpla I'll use...

00:08:35.880 --> 00:08:38.790
﻿This Gunpla is—!

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:42.990
﻿Are you sure, Commodore?

00:08:43.260 --> 00:08:45.590
﻿You just deceived your grandson.

00:08:45.590 --> 00:08:47.430
﻿Whether it's wrong or right,

00:08:47.430 --> 00:08:50.900
﻿I'm not good enough
﻿to defeat the Meijin.

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:53.730
﻿But Julian will...

00:08:55.370 --> 00:08:56.800
﻿My grandson will...!

00:08:57.240 --> 00:08:59.510
﻿You're persistent as always.

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:01.610
﻿I just assessed the battlefield.

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:06.650
﻿I-I had no idea...

00:09:07.820 --> 00:09:11.250
﻿You have no family or
﻿the means to earn money.

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:13.120
﻿You played Gunpla Battle to survive.

00:09:14.590 --> 00:09:18.030
﻿I have a weakness for stories like that.

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:24.260
﻿Aila, you can stay at my house,
﻿until you find someplace to live.

00:09:24.270 --> 00:09:25.600
﻿Really!?

00:09:25.930 --> 00:09:27.400
﻿Yeah!

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:29.240
﻿Besides, if you come to my house,

00:09:29.240 --> 00:09:31.310
﻿you can be with Reiji.

00:09:31.540 --> 00:09:34.170
﻿Wh-What!?

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:36.910
﻿What do you mean "what"?

00:09:36.910 --> 00:09:38.110
﻿How cute.

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:46.690
﻿Grandpa always intended
﻿to give me this machine.

00:09:48.390 --> 00:09:50.560
﻿But it's been three years.

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:52.660
﻿Can I do it?

00:09:52.660 --> 00:09:54.730
﻿Are you looking for an opponent?

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:56.060
﻿You are?

00:09:56.630 --> 00:10:00.470
﻿I'm Mao Yasaka, best 16
﻿in the World Tournament.

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:03.870
﻿If you like,
﻿shall I be your opponent?

00:10:04.440 --> 00:10:05.510
﻿Is that okay?

00:10:05.510 --> 00:10:09.910
﻿I haven't battled for a while,
﻿so I can't wait to fight!

00:10:09.910 --> 00:10:10.810
﻿Thanks.

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:14.410
﻿But what's that Gunpla?

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:16.220
﻿The joints are worn out.

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:18.790
﻿I've used it for a long time.

00:10:22.120 --> 00:10:23.520
﻿Are you ready?

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:25.990
﻿Yeah, I'm all set.

00:10:26.530 --> 00:10:29.130
﻿I need to blow off some steam.

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:33.200
﻿So I'm playing in earnest!

00:10:37.410 --> 00:10:38.310
﻿It's no good.

00:10:39.110 --> 00:10:41.510
﻿With my limited equipment,

00:10:41.510 --> 00:10:44.010
﻿I can't get much data on this gem.

00:10:44.450 --> 00:10:46.080
﻿I'll have to ask my professor...

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:49.820
﻿to get me some help from
﻿this country's research institutes.

00:10:49.820 --> 00:10:51.390
<i>﻿Battle ended.</i>

00:10:53.350 --> 00:10:54.820
﻿A free battle?

00:11:00.230 --> 00:11:01.560
﻿The Gundam X Maoh!

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:05.500
﻿Mao! What happened to you?

00:11:05.770 --> 00:11:07.970
﻿T-Too strong...

00:11:07.970 --> 00:11:08.900
﻿What?

00:11:10.710 --> 00:11:13.840
﻿That Gunpla is a monster.

00:11:15.740 --> 00:11:17.880
﻿We got it working for now, but...

00:11:17.880 --> 00:11:20.780
﻿it's only 80 percent complete.

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:22.150
﻿This will do.

00:11:22.150 --> 00:11:25.550
﻿With this machine's potential,
﻿I could manage as it is.

00:11:25.550 --> 00:11:26.420
﻿Chief Allan.

00:11:27.090 --> 00:11:30.590
﻿Your opponent in the semifinals
﻿has changed their fighter.

00:11:31.060 --> 00:11:32.390
﻿What?

00:11:32.390 --> 00:11:33.530
﻿What's his name?

00:11:33.530 --> 00:11:36.260
﻿His registry name is Julian Mackenzie.

00:11:37.470 --> 00:11:38.730
﻿Julian!?

00:11:38.730 --> 00:11:40.200
﻿Julian Mackenzie!?

00:11:41.370 --> 00:11:42.870
﻿Kawaguchi...!

00:11:42.870 --> 00:11:45.770
﻿Allan, in tomorrow's semifinals...

00:11:47.840 --> 00:11:51.880
﻿We might lose...!

00:11:54.320 --> 00:11:55.780
﻿It's a mess.

00:11:56.050 --> 00:12:00.320
﻿I can't believe any fighter
﻿could hurt Mao's Gunpla so much.

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:02.320
﻿Who the heck did it?

00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:03.960
﻿Someone called Julian.

00:12:05.190 --> 00:12:08.630
﻿He told me he's fighting
﻿in the semifinals tomorrow.

00:12:08.630 --> 00:12:09.760
﻿In the semifinals?

00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:14.000
﻿Which means that person
﻿must be Yuuki's opponent.

00:12:16.370 --> 00:12:18.140
﻿Julian Mackenzie.

00:12:19.040 --> 00:12:22.140
﻿He was the head student of the first class...

00:12:22.140 --> 00:12:25.650
﻿at the Gunpla Academy, an elite
﻿training institution for Gunpla builders.

00:12:25.650 --> 00:12:28.780
﻿Even people with world-level ability
﻿had trouble getting in.

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:32.820
﻿With his genius building skills,

00:12:32.820 --> 00:12:36.060
﻿he was the closest to
﻿being the next Meijin.

00:12:36.060 --> 00:12:36.690
﻿Yeah.

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:42.160
﻿I also thought he was worthy
﻿of being the third Meijin.

00:12:42.430 --> 00:12:46.200
﻿But he suddenly quit the Academy,

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:49.440
﻿and disappeared from
﻿the Gunpla Battle scene.

00:12:49.440 --> 00:12:54.240
﻿Three years later,
﻿the genius has returned.

00:12:54.780 --> 00:12:58.780
﻿Kawaguchi, how many times
﻿did you fight him at the Academy?

00:12:58.780 --> 00:13:00.580
﻿Seven times.

00:13:00.580 --> 00:13:01.450
﻿The results?

00:13:03.020 --> 00:13:04.580
﻿Zero wins, seven losses.

00:13:06.150 --> 00:13:07.490
﻿Total defeat.

00:13:09.160 --> 00:13:11.730
﻿Is it true, Lieutenant!?

00:13:11.730 --> 00:13:12.660
﻿Yeah.

00:13:12.660 --> 00:13:14.590
﻿The third Meijin Kawaguchi is...

00:13:15.100 --> 00:13:16.860
﻿Tatsuya Yuuki.

00:13:16.860 --> 00:13:20.870
﻿He's that youngster you
﻿looked after at the Gunpla Academy.

00:13:21.340 --> 00:13:23.170
﻿No way...

00:13:23.170 --> 00:13:25.540
﻿He loved Gunpla so much.

00:13:26.570 --> 00:13:31.210
﻿Now he's inherited the Meijin name
﻿and the fiendish pursuit of victory?

00:13:31.750 --> 00:13:32.880
﻿Why?

00:13:33.820 --> 00:13:36.550
﻿Why, Tatsuya?

00:13:38.690 --> 00:13:39.750
﻿Julian.

00:13:42.190 --> 00:13:43.660
﻿Why did you quit the Academy!?

00:13:45.660 --> 00:13:48.330
﻿I entered this academy
﻿to enjoy Gunpla.

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:52.500
﻿I couldn't live my life
﻿like the second Meijin,

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:56.400
﻿trampling friends and
﻿making enemies in order to win.

00:13:59.010 --> 00:14:01.580
﻿You can think that I ran away.

00:14:05.050 --> 00:14:06.910
﻿Julian.

00:14:06.910 --> 00:14:11.220
﻿You quit Gunpla
﻿to protect your affection for it.

00:14:11.850 --> 00:14:14.690
﻿But I want to find my own way...

00:14:15.620 --> 00:14:18.960
﻿to keep my love for Gunpla.

00:14:22.730 --> 00:14:23.630
﻿Tatsuya.

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:27.800
﻿Have you been captured
﻿by the second Meijin's ideology?

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:33.510
﻿Wallowing in carnage,
﻿seeking only victory...

00:14:36.510 --> 00:14:40.580
<i>﻿We now begin match two
﻿of the semifinals.</i>

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:43.520
﻿- He's the one Mao told us about.
- ﻿Yeah.

00:14:44.290 --> 00:14:46.450
﻿Mr. Julian Mackenzie.

00:14:47.660 --> 00:14:49.360
﻿Tatsuya.

00:14:51.760 --> 00:14:53.730
﻿Julian.

00:14:54.130 --> 00:14:56.100
﻿I made a promise to Grandpa.

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:58.600
﻿Suddenly, you've become
﻿my greatest obstacle.

00:14:58.800 --> 00:14:59.930
﻿But more than that,

00:14:59.930 --> 00:15:03.100
﻿I want to know why
﻿you became the third Meijin.

00:15:03.400 --> 00:15:05.210
﻿I'll overcome you!

00:15:05.640 --> 00:15:08.640
<i>﻿Beginning Plavsky particle dispersal.</i>

00:15:13.980 --> 00:15:16.080
<i>﻿Field 2, Desert.</i>

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:25.230
﻿Yuuki brought a new Gunpla!

00:15:25.230 --> 00:15:27.990
﻿It's a remodeled Gundam Exia.

00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:31.160
﻿A third-generation mobile suit
﻿developed by...

00:15:31.600 --> 00:15:33.870
﻿the private armed organization
﻿Celestial Being.

00:15:33.870 --> 00:15:35.240
<i>﻿Battle start.</i>

00:15:37.100 --> 00:15:40.770
﻿Meijin Kawaguchi, Amazing Exia,
﻿here I come!

00:15:46.180 --> 00:15:50.820
﻿That's Julian's own machine,
﻿the Gundam F91 Imagine!

00:16:13.140 --> 00:16:14.270
﻿They're not moving.

00:16:14.480 --> 00:16:15.940
﻿No, they are.

00:16:15.940 --> 00:16:16.710
﻿What?

00:16:16.980 --> 00:16:20.510
﻿They've traded blows in their minds
﻿countless times.

00:16:21.350 --> 00:16:25.450
﻿It's so intense I'm getting
﻿goose bumps all over.

00:16:28.220 --> 00:16:29.460
﻿The Exia is on the move!

00:16:30.360 --> 00:16:35.300
﻿Julian Mackenzie's F91 Imagine
﻿is supposedly invincible.

00:16:40.070 --> 00:16:43.670
﻿But it's still an old Gunpla
﻿made three years ago!

00:16:50.780 --> 00:16:51.040
﻿Darn!

00:16:55.280 --> 00:16:57.180
﻿One machine turned into three!?

00:16:57.180 --> 00:16:59.350
﻿They're just afterimages with mass.

00:17:02.020 --> 00:17:04.560
﻿When the F91 moves at high speed,

00:17:04.560 --> 00:17:07.890
﻿the Gunpla's paint peels off
and creates afterimages.

00:17:07.900 --> 00:17:09.930
﻿That's why it seemed to split.

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:12.400
﻿I saw this a long time ago.

00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:16.300
﻿This is why Julian was called
﻿worthy of being the next Meijin.

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:18.270
﻿It's the "Back Jet Stream"!

00:17:23.710 --> 00:17:25.710
﻿You've improved, Tatsuya!

00:17:29.550 --> 00:17:33.720
﻿And you haven't lost your edge!

00:17:42.630 --> 00:17:43.930
﻿Tatsuya!

00:17:43.930 --> 00:17:45.870
﻿Why did you take on the name?

00:17:45.870 --> 00:17:47.830
﻿Have you yielded to
﻿the second Meijin's ideology!

00:17:48.270 --> 00:17:50.440
﻿I'd never do it for such a reason!

00:17:55.440 --> 00:17:57.610
<i>﻿If you have another one, then show me.</i>

00:17:58.880 --> 00:17:59.810
<i>﻿Your belief!</i>

00:18:00.480 --> 00:18:01.720
﻿Your determination!

00:18:02.120 --> 00:18:03.250
﻿He's coming!

00:18:03.250 --> 00:18:06.050
<i>﻿Allan, I'm resigning as Meijin for now.</i>

00:18:06.050 --> 00:18:06.620
﻿What!?

00:18:07.250 --> 00:18:09.820
﻿I'll overcome him as Tatsuya Yuuki!

00:18:11.690 --> 00:18:15.830
﻿By doing so, I'll become
﻿the Meijin I'm aiming for!

00:18:26.370 --> 00:18:27.010
﻿Gotcha!

00:18:29.780 --> 00:18:30.610
﻿Darn!

00:18:37.150 --> 00:18:39.290
﻿Back Jet Stream!

00:18:40.490 --> 00:18:42.690
﻿Turn bright red, Exia!

00:18:44.430 --> 00:18:45.330
﻿Trans-Am!

00:19:42.680 --> 00:19:43.580
<i>﻿Tatsuya!</i>

00:19:49.420 --> 00:19:50.090
﻿Darn!

00:19:52.130 --> 00:19:54.230
<i>﻿This is my...</i>

00:19:55.400 --> 00:19:56.360
﻿determination!

00:20:03.640 --> 00:20:06.570
﻿He met all my attacks.

00:20:07.640 --> 00:20:11.010
﻿This isn't the fighting style
﻿of the second Meijin.

00:20:12.280 --> 00:20:13.680
﻿Tatsuya.

00:20:13.680 --> 00:20:18.850
﻿You dared to become a Meijin
﻿to change the way of Gunpla?

00:20:20.890 --> 00:20:24.320
﻿That's your determination?

00:20:27.600 --> 00:20:29.530
<i>﻿Battle ended.</i>

00:20:31.170 --> 00:20:33.130
﻿It was a splendid battle.

00:20:33.230 --> 00:20:35.240
﻿Wow!

00:20:35.240 --> 00:20:37.540
﻿Reiji is going to fight
﻿someone that strong?

00:20:38.740 --> 00:20:40.910
﻿It's so exciting, Sei.

00:20:40.910 --> 00:20:43.880
﻿That guy's our opponent in the final round.

00:20:44.380 --> 00:20:48.880
﻿How reckless you were.
﻿The Trans-Am isn't adjusted yet.

00:20:48.880 --> 00:20:51.780
﻿That was the only way to win.

00:20:54.320 --> 00:20:56.890
﻿I'm completely defeated, Tatsuya.

00:20:57.160 --> 00:20:58.260
﻿No,

00:20:58.260 --> 00:21:00.790
﻿Meijin Kawaguchi the Third.

00:21:02.600 --> 00:21:04.760
﻿Without these sunglasses,

00:21:04.770 --> 00:21:06.730
﻿I'd have been shot down.

00:21:07.100 --> 00:21:09.900
﻿You should thank the Meijin's costume.

00:21:09.900 --> 00:21:12.640
﻿Julian, won't you come back to Gunpla?

00:21:13.940 --> 00:21:17.080
﻿It was going to be a one-time thing,
﻿but that seems unlikely.

00:21:18.280 --> 00:21:21.480
﻿I can't stay away
﻿from something this fun.

00:21:23.220 --> 00:21:25.820
﻿Meijin, let's battle again someday.

00:21:28.820 --> 00:21:30.460
﻿Of course.

00:21:34.600 --> 00:21:37.960
﻿Julian will play Gunpla again...

00:21:37.970 --> 00:21:41.070
﻿I should thank the third Meijin for that.

00:21:42.140 --> 00:21:45.000
﻿Hey, Sei, what's Trans-Am?

00:21:45.010 --> 00:21:48.170
﻿It's a system that temporarily
﻿triples your particle emission.

00:21:49.040 --> 00:21:52.850
﻿But once it's used up,
﻿the machine's performance plummets.

00:21:53.580 --> 00:21:55.780
﻿Sure sounds like a last resort.

00:21:56.580 --> 00:21:58.480
﻿We'll counter it with the RG System!

00:21:58.890 --> 00:22:00.390
﻿And then well win!

00:22:01.590 --> 00:22:06.530
﻿- We're gonna win the World Tournament!
﻿- We're gonna win the World Tournament!

00:23:43.290 --> 00:23:45.490
﻿My deduction was right after all.

00:23:46.160 --> 00:23:51.160
﻿The gem that Reiji wears is
﻿a Plavsky particle crystal.

00:23:57.490 --> 00:23:58.820
﻿I love Gunpla Battle!

00:23:58.820 --> 00:24:00.720
﻿That's why I have so many friends now.

00:24:00.720 --> 00:24:02.260
Next episode, "Gunpla Eve".

00:24:02.260 --> 00:24:05.020
If only now would last forever.

00:25:01.800 --> 00:25:03.440
﻿I love Gundam.
